agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/returns/A4-review-luna.json:59:      "title": "The commit can retire its only recovery journal before literature data is durable",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/returns/A4-review-luna.json:61:      "reproduction": "Use the import path that writes an artifact and both literature manifests, then model power loss after the topic state, authentication, signing key, and COMMIT_INTENT/retirement directory entries are durable but before the literature blob/manifest file data and parent directories are durable. On restart the journal is gone, while the authenticated state names a literature snapshot whose files may be stale or missing; recovery has no target snapshot available and the literature/state binding fails or has already lost the imported data. The focused suite checks recovery deletion fsync calls and journal retirement, but injects no power-loss boundary around the import writes."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/returns/A4-review-luna.json:68:      "detail": "_remove_retired_transaction unlinks the retiring marker, fsyncs the topic root, and on fsync failure attempts to restore the marker. Restoration errors at lines 1623-1629 are swallowed before the method raises. The storage locks then unwind, and LiteratureBase._topic_transaction_pending sees no active or retiring marker, so an independent writer is allowed to mutate literature while the commit outcome remains unresolved.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/returns/A4-review-luna.json:69:      "reproduction": "In a temporary directory, inject an OSError for the root fsync after the retiring marker is unlinked and independently fail _atomic_write_bytes before it can restore that marker. The runner raises the expected durable-retirement error, but the marker is absent after lock release and a separate LiteratureBase.import_bytes returns IMPORTED. If the non-durable unlink later reappears after a crash, recovery can apply the transaction snapshot and discard that external import. test_retirement_fsync_failure_keeps_external_writer_fenced only exercises successful marker restoration."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:12:      "failure_class": "delimiter-collision-corrupts-durable-manual-identity",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:19:      "detail": "_manual_id_for hashes an unescaped pipe-joined tuple. All contributing fields accept pipe characters. Within one topic, (cursor='c|x', input_id='y') and (cursor='c', input_id='x|y') with the same reason/detail produce the same manual_id. _add_manual then suppresses the second queue record while the second batch result references that ID, and _save_state authenticates the inconsistent state without validating it first.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:20:      "impact": "A valid two-batch input can return successfully, advance the cursor, and persist a state that fails its own manual-queue linkage checks on restart. Structured URI/idempotency composition is fixed, but delimiter-safe identity is not complete.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:21:      "coverage_gap": "No scoped test constructs delimiter-bearing topic/cursor/input/detail tuples or checks collision-free manual IDs."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:35:      "detail": "When an incoming observation is idempotent with a persisted record that has a different observation_id, the first EXISTING_OBSERVED result correctly returns the persisted ID. A later-cursor PROCESSED_INPUT_REPLAY or SEEN_OBSERVATION_KEY branch instead constructs the result with the incoming observation_id, even though its evidence resolves the alternate persisted record.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:36:      "impact": "The same persisted observation is exposed under different result identities across cursor replay paths, and the validator explicitly permits this for duplicate evidence. This breaks stable replay identity without reimporting literature.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:37:      "coverage_gap": "The new integrity test replays only the same stored cursor, while the protected cross-batch duplicate test asserts status/count but not the returned observation_id."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:51:      "impact": "The lock can bind an unintended inode, and a concurrent pathname swap can redirect snapshot reads or recovery writes outside the intended literature root. Advisory locks do not close this non-cooperating filesystem race.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:64:      "impact": "After recovery reports success and removes/fsyncs the transaction journal, a power loss can resurrect a stale nested entry and leave literature bytes inconsistent with the authenticated state with no journal left to repair it.",
