+   295	---
+   296	name: quality-gate-triage
+   297	description: Use when a quality gate, CI check, static guard, test suite, or local verification command fails and the failure needs root-cause triage plus durable prevention.
+   298	---
+   299	
+   300	# Quality Gate Triage
+   301	
+   302	Classify the failing gate, isolate the smallest reproducible failure, fix the root cause, and decide whether the failure class needs a reusable guard or a narrower fixture.
+   303	
+   304	## Procedure
+   305	
+   306	1. Identify the failing command, profile, stage, severity, and touched files.
+   307	2. Classify the failure as product, implementation, contract, data, runtime, visual, accessibility, security, infrastructure, flaky, or guard-logic failure.
+   308	3. Reproduce the smallest failure before editing broad code paths.
+   309	4. Fix the source-of-truth layer first. Do not silence the guard before deciding whether it is wrong.
+   310	5. If the guard is wrong, narrow parser logic, include/exclude scope, trigger conditions, or fixture assumptions.
+   311	6. If the failure class can recur, create or update a guard card before promoting a new blocking guard.
+   312	7. Add red proof and green proof when practical. For runtime, screenshot, and paper-figure work, use a replayable artifact or synthetic broken case when source fixtures are not natural.
+   313	8. Bind the guard to a repair Skill, docs, adapter inputs, and QA evidence when applicable.
+   314	9. Run the narrow guard/test first, then the wider profile or project gate.
+   315	
+   316	## New Guard Checklist
+   317	
+   318	- Failure class is stable beyond the current file or screenshot.
+   319	- Scope is narrow and has include/exclude or trigger rules.
+   320	- Red proof catches the old or synthetic bad case.
+   321	- Green proof protects recommended and legal boundary cases.
+   322	- Failure output contains path, rule, reason, and repair guidance.
+   323	- Cost level is appropriate for the target loop.
+   324	- Evidence output exists for blocking or release gates when practical.
+   325	- The guard card is filled before the guard becomes enforced.
+   326	
+   327	## Output
+   328	
+   329	Report:
+   330	
+   331	- failing guard and command;
+   332	- failure class;
+   333	- root cause;
+   334	- source fix;
+   335	- guard/test change;
+   336	- red/green or negative proof;
+   337	- evidence path;
+   338	- remaining false-positive or lifecycle risk.
