      "path": "matharc/v02/topic_observation.py",
      "line": "2569-2591",
      "title": "A successful commit retires its only recovery journal before target literature is durable",
      "detail": "_save_state durably records the target literature snapshot in COMMIT_INTENT, then writes state, authentication, and signing key and removes the journal without syncing the actual target literature files and directories. LiteratureBase._record at literature_base.py:415-417 and ArtifactStore.put_bytes/save_manifest at artifact_store.py:130-138 and 261-268 only write and replace; they do not fsync file contents or containing directories. Fsyncing the topic root for state, key, and journal entries does not make nested literature data durable. A power loss after run returns can therefore preserve the authenticated state and key while losing or reverting observations.json, the artifact manifest, or a blob. With both journal names durably absent, restart fails integrity checks and has no snapshot from which to recover the committed generation.",
      "reproduction": "Run a first-generation import that creates a new artifact digest prefix on a fault-injection filesystem, allow _save_state to return, then crash while retaining only fsynced writes and directory entries. Preserve the root-level state/authentication/key and journal deletions but discard unsynced literature writes. Restarting TopicObservationRunner fails on missing or mismatched literature, and neither transaction journal exists."
    },
