10921:Because the fresh review found reproducible gate failures, `quality-gate-triage` would normally govern classification. I’m checking only its link target first; if it resolves into the forbidden Harness repository, I will not open it and will keep the review bounded to the already loaded release-verification rules.
10944:description: Use when a quality gate, CI check, static guard, test suite, or local verification command fails and the failure needs root-cause triage plus durable prevention.
10949:Classify the failing gate, isolate the smallest reproducible failure, fix the root cause, and decide whether the failure class needs a reusable guard or a narrower fixture.
10953:1. Identify the failing command, profile, stage, severity, and touched files.
10954:2. Classify the failure as product, implementation, contract, data, runtime, visual, accessibility, security, infrastructure, flaky, or guard-logic failure.
10955:3. Reproduce the smallest failure before editing broad code paths.
10958:6. If the failure class can recur, create or update a guard card before promoting a new blocking guard.
10959:7. Add red proof and green proof when practical. For runtime, screenshot, and paper-figure work, use a replayable artifact or synthetic broken case when source fixtures are not natural.
10965:- Failure class is stable beyond the current file or screenshot.
10969:- Failure output contains path, rule, reason, and repair guidance.
10971:- Evidence output exists for blocking or release gates when practical.
10978:- failing guard and command;
10979:- failure class;
10980:- root cause;
10996:- Temporary reproductions may use a fresh directory under /tmp only and must be removed before return.
