agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:12:      "failure_class": "delimiter-collision-corrupts-durable-manual-identity",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:20:      "impact": "A valid two-batch input can return successfully, advance the cursor, and persist a state that fails its own manual-queue linkage checks on restart. Structured URI/idempotency composition is fixed, but delimiter-safe identity is not complete.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:35:      "detail": "When an incoming observation is idempotent with a persisted record that has a different observation_id, the first EXISTING_OBSERVED result correctly returns the persisted ID. A later-cursor PROCESSED_INPUT_REPLAY or SEEN_OBSERVATION_KEY branch instead constructs the result with the incoming observation_id, even though its evidence resolves the alternate persisted record.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:51:      "impact": "The lock can bind an unintended inode, and a concurrent pathname swap can redirect snapshot reads or recovery writes outside the intended literature root. Advisory locks do not close this non-cooperating filesystem race.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:56:      "failure_class": "nested-directory-delete-not-durably-fsynced",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:63:      "detail": "Recovery unlinks stale literature files at arbitrary nested paths but fsyncs only the literature root afterward. An unlink is durable only when the file's immediate containing directory is fsynced. For example, deleting literature/artifacts/<file> requires fsync of literature/artifacts, not just literature.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:64:      "impact": "After recovery reports success and removes/fsyncs the transaction journal, a power loss can resurrect a stale nested entry and leave literature bytes inconsistent with the authenticated state with no journal left to repair it.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-bdd83e9/returns/A4-review-sol.json:65:      "coverage_gap": "Crash tests simulate Python exceptions and process ordering; they do not verify power-loss durability or fsync calls for every changed directory."
