agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1288:      "detail": "_persisted_observation_for_input selects candidates matching either observation_id or idempotency_key and then chooses by status and lexicographic observation_id. The two identities are not interchangeable: LiteratureBase rejects an observation_id reused for another logical source, and the state validator requires the persisted record selected for duplicate evidence to have the input idempotency key. _save_state authenticates the state but does not run the full state validator before committing it.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1296:      "detail": "ArtifactStore.put_bytes writes the blob and replaces it without fsyncing the blob or its containing directory, save_manifest does the same for manifest.json, and LiteratureBase._record does the same for observations.json at lines 411-417. TopicObservationRunner._save_state snapshots those files, writes and fsyncs the topic transaction/state/authentication/key files, verifies the in-memory snapshot, and then _remove_transaction retires and removes the journal at lines 2582-2591. A root-directory fsync for the topic files is not a durability barrier for the literature files or their nested directories.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1305:      "reproduction": "In a temporary directory, inject an OSError for the root fsync after the retiring marker is unlinked and independently fail _atomic_write_bytes before it can restore that marker. The runner raises the expected durable-retirement error, but the marker is absent after lock release and a separate LiteratureBase.import_bytes returns IMPORTED. If the non-durable unlink later reappears after a crash, recovery can apply the transaction snapshot and discard that external import. test_retirement_fsync_failure_keeps_external_writer_fenced only exercises successful marker restoration."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1312:      "detail": "The 66 focused tests pass, including the alternate persisted-ID replay test and the retirement-fsync test, but they do not combine an observation_id collision with a different persisted idempotency key, do not validate state before _save_state commits it, do not inject failure of retiring-marker restoration, and do not exercise literature blob/manifest fsync ordering through a crash boundary. Passing tests therefore do not establish the claimed identity and durability remediation.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1389:      "detail": "_save_state durably records the target literature snapshot in COMMIT_INTENT, then writes state, authentication, and signing key and removes the journal without syncing the actual target literature files and directories. LiteratureBase._record at literature_base.py:415-417 and ArtifactStore.put_bytes/save_manifest at artifact_store.py:130-138 and 261-268 only write and replace; they do not fsync file contents or containing directories. Fsyncing the topic root for state, key, and journal entries does not make nested literature data durable. A power loss after run returns can therefore preserve the authenticated state and key while losing or reverting observations.json, the artifact manifest, or a blob. With both journal names durably absent, restart fails integrity checks and has no snapshot from which to recover the committed generation.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1390:      "reproduction": "Run a first-generation import that creates a new artifact digest prefix on a fault-injection filesystem, allow _save_state to return, then crash while retaining only fsynced writes and directory entries. Preserve the root-level state/authentication/key and journal deletions but discard unsynced literature writes. Restarting TopicObservationRunner fails on missing or mismatched literature, and neither transaction journal exists."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1405:      "detail": "An out-of-order cursor records a CURSOR_CONFLICT manual entry whose detail is derived from the then-current next_cursor. The runner still permits a later batch at the correct cursor to advance next_cursor and saves that state without validating the produced projection. On reload, the validator recomputes the historical conflict detail using the new next_cursor, or rejects when the manual cursor now equals next_cursor. The valid batch returns successfully even though the newly authenticated state is self-invalidating.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1412:      "title": "A normal pending-to-observed upgrade authenticates historical evidence that the validator rejects",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1413:      "detail": "A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-semantics-retry.log:1414:      "reproduction": "Run c0->c1 with input A using a restricted observation so the result is PENDING. Run c1->c2 with input B using an OPEN SourceObservation with the same observation_id, canonical URI, pinned version, digest, and bytes. LiteratureBase upgrades the record and the second run returns IMPORTED/APPLIED. Constructing a new TopicObservationRunner or reading next_cursor then raises because the first batch says PENDING while the current literature record is OBSERVED."
